            <div xml:id="d422">

                <pb facs="0466" n="366" xml:id="pg366"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">823.032/45: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in Peru</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Smith</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-04-07T17:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 7, 1920—5
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>44. Your April 2, 1 a.m., and March 23, 11 a.m.</p>
                <p>If the question is still a live one, and the Department’s opinion desired, you
                    may state that the Department believes the proposed law might have an
                    unfortunate and disquieting effect, particularly upon foreign investors in
                    Peru.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Colby</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
